 including handling enquiries, maintaining filing systems, and overseeing procurement and financial accounts • Coordinate logistics for workshops, competitions, and related events • Serve as a liaison between ORKT, University departments, students, and external partners • Develop technology marketing initiatives; organise promotional events and marketing activities; and prepare marketing and presentation materials • Coordinate the preparation of reports and data related to entrepreneurship programmes • Maintain and update the database for Lingnan University Xcelerator (LUX) operations, including events, funding, and partner networks • Perform any other duties as assigned by supervisors Requirements • A recognised degree in Sciences and Engineering with at least 3 years’ of in business administration and operations • Experience in organising marketing or promotional events • A customer service oriented mindset with strong attention to detail and the ability to multitask effectively • Excellent interpersonal and communication skills in both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua) • Strong analytical, organisational, and problem solving skills • A passion for building and supporting innovative technology startups • Travelling and site visits may be occasionally required Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits and mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only . We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by 