245) The School of Graduate Studies is established for strengthening the central support for postgraduate programmes as well as the monitoring of their quality in alignment with the University’s strategic direction of expanding and providing quality postgraduate education. It also proactively seeks collaboration with leading institutions in the international academic communities to co-organise scholarly activities to enhance postgraduate student learning. Responsibilities • Provide a wide range of support to matters pertaining to postgraduate studies, including student admissions and publicity, registration, maintenance of student records, assessment and financial sponsorships • Provide support in general office administration • Provide counter services • Handle student enquiries • Provide logistical support to meetings, events and activities • Perform any other duties as assigned by the supervisor(s) Requirements • A Bachelor’s degree • 1-2 years of administrative experience, preferably in tertiary institutions (those with more than 3 years’ experience will be considered for the post of Administrative Officer) • Good logical thinking, analytical, coordination and problem-solving skills • Good interpersonal and communication skills • A good command of written and verbal English and Chinese (both Cantonese and Putonghua) • A strong sense of responsibility • Able to work independently and under tight schedules • High proficiency in MS office applications and other IT applications Candidates with less/more experience will also be considered for appointment at a relevant rank. Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
