    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3099?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Research Officer (Computational Text Analysis and Qualitative Research), SOCSP",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Research Officer (Computational Text Analysis and Qualitative Research), SOCSP Hong Kong, China | req3099 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/30/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Research Officer (Computational Text Analysis and Qualitative Research) Department of Sociology and Social Policy (Post Ref.: 26/243 ) The appointee will join an interdisciplinary research team, led by Prof. Alex Preda, bringing together expertise in economic sociology, financial technology, computer science, data science and blockchain analytics. The project is Trustworthy Stablecoins: Coordinating Centralized and Decentralized Finance at Scale . The appointee will contribute to a mixed-methods study combining computational text analysis, qualitative document analysis and interviews to examine trust, evidence and reporting in stablecoin markets and the interface between centralized and decentralized finance. The position is for a period of 18 months, starting 2 January 2027. Responsibilities • Collect, construct, clean and manage textual datasets comprising regulatory documents, court and litigation documents, audit and reserve reports, industry white papers, technical documentation and related materials • Conduct computational text analysis using appropriate programming and natural-language-processing techniques • Conduct qualitative content/thematic analysis of documentary materials and integrate computational and qualitative findings • Assist with the design and conduct of semi-structured interviews with participants in financial, fintech and blockchain-related fields, including interview data management, coding and analysis • Contribute to the interpretation of findings, preparation of research outputs, presentations and academic publications • Maintain well-documented and reproducible research • Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor Requirements • A master’s degree in one of the following: sociology, economic sociology, computational social science, digital social science, anthropology, communication/information studies, behavioural science, or a related social science discipline. Candidates from closely related interdisciplinary fields will also be considered • Demonstrated experience in analysing qualitative or textual data, with experience in computational text analysis, text mining or natural-language processing, preferably using Python and/or R • Experience in the collection, cleaning, organisation and analysis of unstructured textual data and document corpora • Strong qualitative research skills, including qualitative textual analysis; experience with semi-structured interviewing and thematic coding would be an advantage • Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary research team and to maintain clear and reproducible research documentation • Excellent written and spoken English • Knowledge of financial markets, financial institutions, fintech, blockchain or digital assets would be an advantage Salary and Benefits Commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits and mandatory provident fund. Appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract for 18 months. Application Procedure (online applications only) Please click \"Apply Now\" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/2995?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Senior Manager/Manager (Administrative Support and Institutional Risk), OCCBGA",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Manager/Manager (Administrative Support and Institutional Risk), OCCBGA Hong Kong, China | req2995 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/25/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Senior Manager (Administrative Support and Institutional Risk) / Manager (Administrative Support and Institutional Risk) Office of Council/Court Business and Governance Administration (Post Ref.: 26/145) Responsibilities • Lead end-to-end secretariat support for Council and Court, including agenda planning, paper quality assurance, records and minute-keeping, action tracking, and follow-up • Support induction and ongoing development for Council and Court members; maintain register of interests and compliance with relevant codes • Lead the institutional risk management framework, including risk classification, appetite statements, methodology, and reporting cadence • Coordinate risk identification, assessment, and mitigation planning with senior management and risk owners; maintain the institutional risk register • Maintain the governance calendar, policy inventory, and review cycles; coordinate cross-unit policy updates and approvals • Develop and maintain a policy information portal to host, manage, and update organizational policies, ensuring compliance and easy employee or user access • Liaise with external stakeholders, including the HKSAR Government, UGC, LegCo, and other partners • Draft high-quality correspondence to government officials, distinguished scholars, and community leaders; and • Perform other duties as assigned Requirements • Bachelor’s degree with at least 10 years of relevant post-degree experience, including 5 years in a supervisory role, preferably in corporate governance, administration, or quality assurance within tertiary institutions or public bodies • Proven experience in committee/secretariat work, including drafting policy papers, reports, proposals, minutes, and speeches; experience in the higher education sector in Hong Kong would be an advantage • Strong analytical, problem-solving, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently and under pressure • Highly organised, detail-oriented, and capable of managing multiple priorities effectively • Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua) • Good IT literacy Candidates with less/more experience will be considered for appointment at a relevant rank. Salary and Benefits Commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the posts are filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3097?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow (MSoDA), Department of Sociology and Social Policy",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Postdoctoral Fellow (MSoDA), Department of Sociology and Social Policy Hong Kong, China | req3097 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/18/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Postdoctoral Fellow (MSoDA) Department of Sociology and Social Policy (Post Ref.: 26/241 ) The Department of Sociology and Social Policy brings together scholars with international research experience and publication records in major outlets in Sociology and Social Policy. The Department is a recipient of the University’s Research Excellence Award and Teaching Excellence Awards. We offer teaching in Sociology and Social Policy, the Health and Social Services Management Major and co-host the Social and Public Policy Studies Major with the Department of Economics. The Department hosts an MSocSc Programme in Comparative Social Policy (International) (IMCSP), and an MSocSc Programme in Sociology and Data Analytics (MSoDA), and has been successful in attracting MPhil and PhD students from around the world, as well as Hong Kong PhD Fellows, and winning other external competitive grants. For more information, applicants are advised to visit the departmental website , UG programme website , IMCSP programme website , MSoDA Programme website , and RGC Funding Schemes website . General Requirements Applicants should have obtained / been conferred a PhD degree in Sociology, Social Policy or any discipline related to computational social science, or an equivalent qualification for no more than three years prior to the commencement of the appointment, with relevant teaching and research experience. Applicants are required to provide their research portfolio, publication record, and teaching evaluation among other relevant information. Excellent communication and presentation skills in English are essential. Experience with research utilizing computational methods will be a distinct advantage. The appointee should be able to take up teaching duties in some of the courses on the MSocSc Programme in Sociology and Data Analytics, including but not limited to: “Data Analytics for Social Research”, “Applied Analytical Statistics for Social Scientists”, “Machine Learning with Social Data” and “Social Networks Analysis” . The appointee should be prepared to actively support the coordination and development of our teaching programmes, as well as the research endeavours of faculty members in the areas of Sociology and Social Policy. The appointee is expected to have a strong commitment to academic excellence and engagement in high-quality research and publication, and to submit applications for RGC grants, other local/overseas competitive grants and/or fellowship schemes. Appointment The conditions of appointment will be competitive. The remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, gratuity, incoming passage and baggage allowance for the eligible appointee. The appointment will normally be made on a fixed-term contract of up to two years. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \"Apply Now\" to submit your application. Applicants shall provide names and contact information of at least three referees to whom applicants’ consent has been given for their providing references. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. The review of applications will start from October 2026 and will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3057?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Information Manager, ITSC",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Information Manager, ITSC Hong Kong, China | req3057 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/18/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Information Manager Information Technology Services Centre (Post Ref.: 26/205) Responsibilities Lead and manage the database services team, provide technical guidance and resource allocation to ensure the stable and efficient operation of all database and application systems Oversee the plan, architecture, and execution of the new ERP system setup, with a primary focus on database migration, data integrity, performance optimization, and seamless cutover from legacy systems Manage, maintain, and continuously improve the performance, availability, and security of mission-critical application systems and database infrastructure Provide technical support for UNIX and Linux system administration, including system setup, configuration, third-party software installation, patch upgrades, system monitoring, and health checks Implement and maintain robust database and system backup strategies, disaster recovery (DR) plans, and high-availability (HA) solutions to ensure business continuity and minimize downtime Collaborate with application development teams to optimize database schema design, complex PL/SQL, and index strategies to achieve maximum application efficiency Troubleshoot and resolve complex system and database incidents, perform root cause analysis (RCA), and implement preventive measures to avoid recurrence Maintain and enforce stringent system and database security procedures, including access control, role-based permissions, data encryption, and vulnerability management to comply with organizational policies and audit requirements Manage the lifecycle of systems and databases, including version upgrades, capacity planning, and storage management to support future growth Work in shifts and irregular hours as required Performing any other duties as assigned by supervisors Qualifications and Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Information Systems or a related discipline Minimum 10 years of experience in system administration and database administration, with at least 2 years in a team leadership or supervisory capacity Excellent system and database troubleshooting skills Proficiency in Linux/Unix system administration In-depth knowledge of RDBMS, including installation, configuration, performance tuning, and administration Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively across development and infrastructure teams Hands-on experience in script programming such as Linux shell script, Python, Perl or C will be an advantage Candidates with less/more experience will also be considered for appointment at the relevant rank. Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only . We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified . Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3096?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Administrative Officer, Department of Cultural Studies",
