/ ) offers a Bachelor of Arts (Hons) in Cultural Studies with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. It admits postgraduate research students leading to the award of MPhil and PhD degrees. Since 2003, it has been offering a self-financed taught programme leading to the Master degree of Cultural Studies. The department’s faculty also contribute to the work of the affiliated Centre for Cultural Research and Development ( https://www.ln.edu.hk/cultural/research-centre/ccrd ). Responsibilities • Providing administrative support to matters pertaining to undergraduate programme administration including student admissions, data management and teaching support • Assisting in coordinating seminars and student activities • Providing front-line support to the office • Liaising with internal and external parties to provide logistic support to the Programme • Performing other duties as assigned • Be required to work outside normal office hours occasionally Requirements • A recognized bachelor’s degree or an equivalent qualification • At least two years’ full-time relevant work experience in tertiary education institutions. Experience in student admissions and academic programme support would be an advantage • Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese and Putonghua) • Proficiency in PC operations (MS Office applications, Adobe Acrobat / Creative Cloud applications, updating and maintaining website) • Good communication and interpersonal skills • Ability to work independently, effectively and efficiently Salary and Benefits Commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
