ster of Arts in Digital History in Global Asia Programme. Besides the day-to-day programme operations, the appointee will lead the promotional efforts of the programme to recruit high-quality applicants from Hong Kong, Mainland China, and overseas. Responsibilities • Lead promotional efforts for the programme to prospective students in Hong Kong, Mainland China, and overseas, including outreach, marketing, and engagement activities • Administer all aspects of the Taught Master of Arts Programme ‘Digital History in Global Asia’ • Provide logistical and administrative support for seminars, events, and programme activities • Assist the Programme Director in compiling programme-level reports • Offer administrative assistance to faculty members and students • Manage daily operations of the Programme Office • Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor Requirements • A recognized Bachelor’s degree (or above); a postgraduate degree is an advantage • Relevant experience, especially in the tertiary education sector, is an advantage • Relevant experience in academic programme marketing is an advantage • Computer literacy, especially familiarity with social media platforms and website development • A background in historical studies and/or digital humanities is an advantage • High proficiency in written and spoken English; proficiency in Chinese (Cantonese and/or Putonghua) is an advantage • Good communication and interpersonal skills with a strong sense of responsibility • Ability to carry out duties independently and efficiently with minimum supervision Salary and Benefits Commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits and mandatory provident fund. Appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract for up to 9 to 11 months. Application Procedure (online applications only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
