counting Manager • Issue debit notes for tuition fees, hostel fees and other expenses to students, and monitor outstanding balances • Update receipts from various collection methods to ensure accurate reflection of all bank transactions • Handle inquiries from students and other departments • Prepare year-end reports to facilitate statutory audits and assist the supervisor in preparing tuition and hostel income budgets • Supervise and provide guidance to the subordinates • Prepare cash flow forecasts and bank reconciliations and provide support for treasury functions • Support supervisors in ERP implementation, system enhancements, and continuous process improvements • Carry out any other duties as assigned by the supervisor Requirements • A recognized Degree or equivalent qualifications in Accounting or related disciplines • Qualified Accountant with professional qualification of HKICPA or equivalent is preferred • Relevant experience in managing accounts receivables and preparing analyses • Knowledge of accounting system implementation/enhancements and process improvement is an advantage • A good team player with strong analytical and communication skills • Able to work under pressure and meet deadlines with multi-tasking skills • Proficiency in MS Office applications • Immediate available is an advantage The appointee will be assigned to work in the Tsuen Wan area. Salary and Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
