    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3087?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Library Officer (Learning Support), Library",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Library Officer (Learning Support), Library Hong Kong, China | req3087 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/7/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Assistant Library Officer (Learning Support) Library (Post Ref.: 26/231) Responsibilities Provide clerical and logistical support to the smooth running of information literacy programs including orientations, workshops, and all other reference and instruction services in both online and in-person formats for the Lingnan community. Assist in conducting library tours, handling enquiries at the service counter and via other channels, and other public services. Assist in managing and coordinating the operations of Course Readings @ Library service. Keep the content of the library website and digital learning objects up-to-date. Prepare promotional materials for workshops and events, and provide supports in all publicity activities. Gather and record statistics, and compile different surveys, statistics and usage report for departmental use. Supervise part-time and student helpers. Perform other duties as assigned by supervisors and University Librarian. Shift duties on evenings, weekends and public holidays will be required. Requirements A good honour Bachelor degree; 1-2 years of working experience preferably in academic libraries with positive customer service attitude; Good command of English and Chinese (including Cantonese and Putonghua); Ability to work in teams and independently; Proficiency in PC skills, with graphic design software knowledge and website authoring experience preferred; Knowledge of 3D modelling, 3D printing, 3D scanning, laser cutting and engraving is preferred; Diploma / Certificate in library service or equivalent is an added advantage. Candidates with less/more experience will also be considered for appointment at the relevant rank. Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only . We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified . Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3083?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Senior Administrative Officer / Administrative Officer, Office of the Faculty of Business",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Administrative Officer / Administrative Officer, Office of the Faculty of Business Hong Kong, China | req3083 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/6/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Senior Administrative Officer / Administrative Officer Office of the Faculty of Business (Post Ref.: 26/227 ) The Faculty of Business is an AACSB-accredited one aiming at continuous improvements of our academic level and education service in the liberal arts setting. The Faculty plays an important role in educating students about cutting-edge, practical knowledge and skills, improving students' academic and professional capabilities, as well as enhancing students' awareness on social responsibilities. Furthermore, we have been devoting every effort to the sustainable development of Lingnan University in the academic community and the substantive realization of our values and mission in the Hong Kong society and the world. The appointee is expected to take up a wide range of administrative duties to the Faculty of Business. Major duties include but are not limited to: Responsibilities • Assist the Director in planning and administering various research and knowledge-transfer projects and activities, as well as managing day-to-day operation of research centre(s) under Hong Kong Institute of Business Studies (HKIBS) • Provide support to matters pertaining to research postgraduate programmes and postdoctoral training of the Faculty and the unit(s) • Work on MoUs and/or agreements with external parties • Liaise with internal and external parties, including but not limited to universities and industry partners from Hong Kong, Chinese Mainland and aboard • Prepare annual report, other reports and data reporting to various units of the university • Perform other duties as assigned by supervisor(s) The appointee may also be required to undertake certain administrative duties for the Faculty of Business and HKIBS. Requirements • A bachelor’s degree or above with at least two years of relevant administrative experience. Preference with be given to candidates with work experience in serving a liaison with universities in Chinese Mainland • A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua) • Strong communication and interpersonal skills • Proficiency in IT and computer applications (e.g., such as MS Office and content management system, etc.) will be an advantage Candidates with less experience will be considered for appointment at a lower rank. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test. Applicants should provide a CV, a cover letter and information about their work experience and academic qualifications. Appointment Commencing salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will start from mid-September 2026 and continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3081?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, School of Graduate Studies",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate Professor, School of Graduate Studies Hong Kong, China | req3081 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Associate Professor School of Graduate Studies (Post Ref.: 26/225) The School of Graduate Studies (GS) was established to strengthen the central support for postgraduate programmes and monitor their quality in alignment with the University’s strategic direction of expanding and providing quality postgraduate education in the digital era. To directly provide professional education for the wider society, the GS also offers a diverse range of Taught Postgraduate (TPg) programmes under three academic clusters: 1. Policy and Education Leadership Cluster, covering public administration, policy studies, and higher education management; 2. Regional Development and Urban Studies Cluster, focusing on regional development, and urban governance, housing studies, and arts and heritage management; and 3. Health, Ageing and Social Innovation Cluster, addressing health services management, ageing studies, gerontechnology, and social innovation and entrepreneurship. To support the continuous growth of GS TPg programmes, the School is now inviting applications for the post of Associate Professor. The appointee is expected to possess research and teaching experiences in one or more of the following areas: • Policy studies • Social policy • Education policy • Higher education management • Health and social care policy • Urban policy The appointee will be expected to (a) conduct high-quality research in the state-of-the-art areas in the area(s) specified above; (b) secure external competitive research grants in various funding bodies; (c) teach multiple subjects in postgraduate-level programmes in the area(s) specified above; (d) recruit and supervise research prostrgraduate students; (e) work on the promotions and admissions as well as the operations for postgraduate programmes; (f) contribute to academic programme/course development; and (g) contribute to other administrative duties as required by the Dean or Associate Dean of GS. General Requirements Applicants should have (i) a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline such as policy studies, public administration, education management, or other relevant areas; (ii) a strong publication record and outstanding citation counts in the specific area(s); (iii) a track record in securing external research grants; (iv) good experience in teaching and programme administration in the specific area(s); (v) excellent interpersonal, organisational and communication skills; and (vi) good command of English and Chinese (including Putonghua). At least six years of relevant experience in the tenure-track academic post is expected. Preference will be given to candidates with outstanding academic training and international exposure. Enquiries shall be directed to the Associate Dean of the School, Professor Simon YAU (yungyau@ln.edu.hk). Appointment The conditions of appointments will be competitive. The rank and remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, gratuity and incoming passage and baggage allowance for the eligible appointees. Appointments will normally be made on a fixed-term contract of up to three years. Appointment will normally be made on an initial contract of three years, which, subject to review and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment with possibility of consideration for substantiation. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Applicants shall provide names and contact information of at least three referees to whom applicants’ consent has been given for their providing references. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3002?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Learning Enhancement, CITAL",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Manager, Learning Enhancement, CITAL Hong Kong, China | req3002 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest-established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well-positioned to take the lead as a comprehensive university of arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovation. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies, and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Assistant Manager, Learning Enhancement (at the rank of Assistant Manager I) Centre for Innovative Teaching and Learning (Post Ref.: 26/151) Responsibilities • Plan and implement professional development workshops and curriculum to develop Lingnan academic staff as leaders in the provision of innovative pedagogy via a comprehensive professional development framework and implementation strategy • Support the initiatives of academic units to develop or revise courses/programmes as related to the delivery of an engaging, personalised, and digitally enriched Outcome-based Education (OBE) curriculum • Contribute to the communities of best practice and working groups and provide relevant pedagogical input to this work • Develop, implement, and evaluate various self-paced learning and workshops related to enriching the learning skills and competencies of students • Support the Learning Enhancement and Learning Design strategic priorities and perform the assigned tasks of the Teaching Development and Language Enhancement Grant (TDLEG) and other UGC-funded Grants • Perform any other duties as assigned by supervisor(s) Requirements • A Bachelor’s Degree with normally 7 years’ relevant work experience • Strong organisational, team, and communication skills, with excellent writing skills in English • Experience in managing and contributing to teaching and learning initiatives • Relevant experience in facilitating professional development for academic staff across a range of learning and teaching areas, such as 21st Century Approaches to Learning and Teaching, Curriculum, Assessment, and OBE, with a thorough understanding of practice and theory of OBE and Qualification Framework of Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People’s Republic of China • Relevant experience in supporting teaching and learning institutional change/pedagogical support for academic staff in innovative pedagogies across the use of technology, online portfolios, curriculum, assessment, and OBE of higher education • Excellent presentation skills, with teaching experience as an advantage • Extensive understanding of current trends in technology-enhanced learning Candidates with less/more experience will be considered for appointment at a relevant rank. Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only . We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified . Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3078?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Senior Research Officer, Division of Science",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Research Officer, Division of Science Hong Kong, China | req3078 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/27/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Senior Research Officer Division of Science (Post Ref.: 26/221 ) The Division of Science ( http://www.LN.edu.hk/dos ) would like to invite applications for the above-mentioned post. The appointee will join a joint research team bringing together the Freshwater Biodiversity & Ecosystem Functioning Lab (led by Dr. Alphonse Tsang) and Applied Ecology and Conservation Laboratory (led by Dr. Roger Lee). The candidate will play a key role in managing an aquatic insect conservation project in South Lantau’s freshwater marshes. Responsibilities • Conduct field surveys in freshwater marshes to establish an ecological baseline for aquatic insects • Curate and digitize aquatic insect specimen collections • Establish a DNA barcoding library for aquatic insects in freshwater marshes • Conduct and advance environmental DNA (eDNA) methods in freshwater marshes • Oversee project progress and prepare progress reports • Prepare educational and public outreach materials to promote aquatic insect conservation • Perform other education- and research-related duties assigned Requirements • A recognized master’s degree (or above) in earth/environmental sciences, life sciences, biology, or a related discipline • Proven field survey and data analytics experience, with a strong passion for ecological research and biodiversity conservation • An outstanding level of physical fitness, including the ability to conduct demanding, full-day outdoor fieldwork carrying equipment in freshwater marshes • Knowledge and experience in bioinformatics and eDNA analysis are a plus • Strong organization and communication skills (both written and spoken) to compile research data for reporting, creating clear public educational content, and communicate effectively with diverse stakeholders Applicants with prior experience in bioinformatics and ecological surveys are highly encouraged to apply for this position. Salary and Benefits Commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, and mandatory provident fund. Appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract for 12 months with the possibility of a further extension on related research projects. Application Procedure Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/2643?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "HPC System Administrator, ITSC",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) HPC System Administrator, ITSC Hong Kong, China | req2643 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/26/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: HPC System Administrator Information Technology Services Centre (Post Ref.: 25/52) Responsibilities • Perform system administration tasks for various Linux distributions • Oversee daily operations of High-Performance Computing (HPC) computing facilities, ensuring smooth and efficient functioning • Manage user accounts and access to HPC resources running on Linux systems • Manage and setup hardware and software for the HPC system • Conduct regular health checks on all systems to proactively identify, resolve, or escalate issues • Provide support to faculty members, students and other users of the HPC systems • Assist users with job submission, scheduling and optimisation • Work shifts and irregular hours as required • Perform any other duties as requested by supervisors Requirements • A recognized bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or a related discipline • At least 3 years of relevant work experience • Proven experience in managing sizable Linux operating environments • Proficiency with Linux/Unix operating systems, file systems and shell commands • Proficiency with the installation of various Linux distributions, such as RHEL, Rocky, Ubuntu and Debian, from scratch • Familiar with tools for installing and managing research software such as conda and docker/singularity • Preferably with knowledge of HPC job schedulers such as Slurm • Willing to learn HPC skills and technologies • Good problem-solving skills • Good communication and interpersonal skills for effective user support • Ability to work independently and as part of a team Candidates with less/more experience will be considered for appointment at a relevant rank. Salary and Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified . Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3075?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Human Resources Officer, Human Resources Office",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Human Resources Officer, Human Resources Office Hong Kong, China | req3075 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Assistant Human Resources Officer Human Resources Office (Fixed term contract of 2 years) (Post Ref.: 26/222) Responsibilities • Provide administrative support to the Human Resources Office • Assist in the co-ordination and administration of various HR-related projects • Provide support to the daily operations of the Office • Perform any other duties as assigned by supervisor(s) Requirements • Post-secondary qualification or above • Relevant working experience in sizable organizations, preferably in the higher education sector • Good spoken and written English and Chinese (including Putonghua) • Good interpersonal and communication skills • Strong sense of responsibility Salary and Benefits Commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Appointment will normally be made on a fixed-term contract of 2 years, with the possibility of renewal subject to mutual agreement and the availability of the post. Application Procedure (online applications only) Please click “Apply Now” to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the posts are filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3074?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Associate Professor / Assistant Professor, Department of English",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate Professor / Assistant Professor, Department of English Hong Kong, China | req3074 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Associate Professor / Assistant Professor Department of English (Post Ref.: 26/220 ) The Department of English ( http://www.LN.edu.hk/eng/ ) of Lingnan University now invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Associate/Assistant Professor specializing in Modern Literature. The appointee is expected to: 1. teach relevant courses at both the undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including supervising undergraduate and/or postgraduate final projects; 2. generate research outputs with high impact and participate in competitive grant applications exercises; and 3. assist the Department with administration and curriculum development. Requirements Applicants for the position should have: (i) a PhD degree in Modern Literature or a relevant area (ii) good track record of publications, grants, and awards (iii) some experience in teaching or developing courses in digital humanities, modern literature or world literatures An appointee at the level of Associate / Assistant Professor should, besides being an effective teacher, demonstrate great potential to produce quality research output in the very near future. Lingnan University is fully committed to the pursuit of excellence in both teaching and research. Candidates are required to provide evidence of quality teaching and information on their research records. Appointment The conditions of appointment will be competitive. The rank and remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, gratuity and incoming passage and baggage allowance for the eligible appointee. Appointment will normally be made on an initial contract of three years, which, subject to review and mutual agreement, may normally lead to longer-term appointment with possibility of consideration for substantiation. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Applicants shall provide names and contact information of at least three referees to whom applicant's consent has been given for their providing references. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3048?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Senior Project Officer, Office of Service-Learning",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Project Officer, Office of Service-Learning Hong Kong, China | req3048 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/18/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Senior Project Officer Office of Service-Learning (Post Ref.: 26/197) The Office of Service-Learning (OSL) is seeking creative, self-motivated, and independent educators to lead the design, development and delivery of innovative programmes at undergraduate (UG) and postgraduate levels. The appointee will play a key role in shaping strategic directions for programme development, promotion and marketing, teaching and learning enhancement, course evaluation, international partnership development, and engagement with industry and professional bodies. The successful candidate is also expected to drive impactful Service-Learning initiatives, foster interdisciplinary collaboration, and contribute to the continuous advancement of the University's educational mission. Responsibilities: • Assist Programme Managers in overseeing day-to-day programme administration and operations • Coordinate co-curriculum learning programmes, including local Service-Learning initiatives and internship opportunities for UG students • Organize and manage interdisciplinary overseas programmes and experiential learning activities for UG students • Liaise with faculty members, community partners, NGOs and industry stakeholders to develop and implement high-impact Service-Learning projects • Build and maintain networks with international partners to develop collaborative courses and programmes • Prepare proposals for grant applications and funding initiatives • Prepare programme reports, funding reports, project evaluations, outcome assessments, and other documentation required for quality assurance, accreditation, and stakeholder reporting • Perform any other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Office Requirements: • Bachelor’s degree with solid qualitative analytical experience; a full-time Master’s or PhD is highly preferred • At least 4 years relevant experience in the education sector • Proven experience in organizing and managing overseas programmes, study tours, Service-Learning projects, or summer camps in the higher education sector • Excellent interpersonal, organizational, resources management and communication skills • Excellent command of both written and spoken English • Demonstrated willingness to spearhead AI and technology-enabled Service-Learning (S-L) initiatives • Undertake overseas travel, including to remote and under-resourced regions, to oversee project delivery, engage community partners, and support student learning and development • Site visits and work irregular hours may be occasionally required, including evenings, weekends, and public holidays • Proven track record of establishing and maintaining partnerships with NGOs is advantageous Candidate with less experience will be considered for the position at the rank of Officer. Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only . We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified . Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
