trative support for academic planning and development, scholarly events and global engagement of the Division • Handle teaching and learning administration matters, involve coordination of teaching timetable and teaching remissions etc • Provide support to the Person in Charge of Division in planning and development of the Division • Serve on committees and other working groups and/or task forces • Assist with division finance planning and handle reimbursement and payments • Perform any other duties as assigned by the Person in Charge of Division or her delegates Requirements • A recognised degree with relevant post-qualification work experience, preferably in programme administration within a higher education setting • Excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese • Excellent liaison, organisational and problem-solving skills • Display a high level of responsibility, independence and professionalism in managing multiple priorities • Positive working attitude and the ability to work well as a team player Salary and Benefits The commencing salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3059?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor, Department of Digital Arts and Creative Industries",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Research Assistant Professor, Department of Digital Arts and Creative Industries Hong Kong, China | req3059 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/28/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Research Assistant Professor Department of Digital Arts and Creative Industries ( Post Ref.: 26/206) The Department of Digital Arts and Creative Industries (DACI) provides conceptual and practical training for students seeking careers in the burgeoning creative and cultural industries in Hong Kong, Greater Bay Area, and beyond. The Department offers three BA (Hon) programmes (Animation and Digital Arts; Film and Visual Arts; Creative Media Industries) and two MA programmes (Creative and Media Industries; Curating and Art History). The appointee will teach a wide range of subjects including animation, digital arts and immersive media, film and media studies, art history and curation. For more information about the programmes, please visit https://www.ln.edu.hk/daci/ . DACI is inviting applications for fixed-term position of Research Assistant Professor to contribute to teaching and development of the Taught Master Programmes: MA in Curating and Art History (MACAH) and MA in Creative and Media Industries (MACMI). The appointee is expected to: i) teach courses in two of the following areas: art history, curating, media and creative industries; ii) student recruitment and admission, and iii) contribute to the research productivity of the Department and apply for RGC grants. Requirements Applicants for the position should have: (i) A PhD degree in art history, museum studies, or creative/media industries; (ii) Good track record of referred publications, awards or competitive grants; (iii) Experience or strong capability in teaching postgraduate courses and supervising student capstone projects; (iv) Familiarity with regional creative landscapes, including East Asian art, media, and creative industries. (v) Ability to teach material culture, art and aesthetics, East Asian creative industries or AI and creative industries will have an advantage. Candidates should have obtained / been conferred a PhD degree or an equivalent qualification for no more than five years prior to the commencement of the appointment. Appointment The conditions of appointment will be competitive. The remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, gratuity, and incoming passage and baggage allowance for the eligible appointee. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \"Apply Now\" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3055?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager I, Office of Global Education",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Manager I, Office of Global Education Hong Kong, China | req3055 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/24/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Assistant Manager I Office of Global Education (Post Ref.: 26/203) Responsibilities • Assist in data collection and reporting of the Office • Provide administrative support to budgeting, reporting, data collection and personal data privacy matters of the Office • Provide administrative and secretarial support to committees and alliances which the University takes part in • Manage and administer student exchange programmes and liaise with internal and external stakeholders • Assist in the overall planning and execution of the University's non-local student recruitment strategies • Organize a wide spectrum of promotional activities to prospective non-local students, foster sustainable relationships with overseas feeder schools • Work closely with the University's UG Admissions team • Perform other duties as assigned by supervisor(s) Requirements • A Bachelor's degree with at least 10 years' relevant work experience • Proficient in written and verbal English and other European language(s) would be an advantage • Excellent interpersonal and communication skills • Excellent organizational and multitasking skills • Experience in working in higher education and dealing with counterparts from diverse backgrounds would be an advantage • Strong analytical skills with knowledge in data analytic/statistical software • Sound knowledge of student exchange and campus inclusion is preferred Candidates with less/more experience will also be considered for appointment at the relevant rank. Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only . We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for 