nsulting and Counselling Psychology Research Centre is seeking an Assistant Research Officer / Research Officer to provide research and administrative support, with a primary focus on coordination and liaison work. Responsibilities • Coordinate and support the Centre’s programmes and projects, including planning and running training classes, workshops, seminars, and related activities • Liaise with companies, schools, universities, and partner institutions • Assist in literature search and review • Conduct data collection and analysis • Assist in the preparation of reports and manuscripts • Occasional travel outside Hong Kong may be required • Perform any other duties as assigned by the Centre Director Requirements • Bachelor’s degree (or above) in psychology or a related discipline; candidates with more relevant experience may be considered for appointment at the Research Officer rank • Experience in project management or programme coordination • Knowledge of counselling psychology, positive psychology, or wellbeing interventions is an advantage • Knowledge of and experience in using SPSS; familiarity with other statistical software such as R or Python is an advantage • Strong sense of responsibility and effective communication skills • Strong command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including fluency in both Cantonese and Putonghua Salary and Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Appointment will be made on contract basis for a period of 12 to 24 months, subject to operational and project needs. Application Procedure (online applications only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
