      "title": "Information Manager (Virtualisation Services), ITSC",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Information Manager (Virtualisation Services), ITSC Hong Kong, China | req2805 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/15/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Information Manager (Virtualisation Services) Information Technology Services Centre (Post Ref.: 25/237) Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible for (i) overall planning, evaluation, implementation and management of the server virtualization infrastructure and Hyper Converged Infrastructure (HCI), including SAN storage and SAN switches; (ii) capacity/performance planning, life cycle control/management of virtualisation hardware, software and virtual machines; (iii) development and management of the campus-wide IoT infrastructure; (iv) preparing and maintaining the backup policies for virtual machines; (v) overseeing miscellaneous network supporting systems including DNS system, mail gateways, network and server monitoring tools, etc.; (vi) working with other ITSC teams in the development and management of on-campus and off-campus backup and recovery systems; (vii) working with other ITSC teams in the development and management of the container and orchestration infrastructure; and (viii) other tasks as assigned by supervisors. The appointee is also required to work in shifts and irregular hours. Requirements Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor's Degree or above in Computer Science; Information Technology, Information Engineering or equivalent; preferably a higher degree in relevant disciplines; (ii) at least 8 years of relevant IT experience, with preferably 3 years in management or a similar role; (iii) strong technical skill and solid hands-on experience with enterprise-grade virtualization technologies (VMware, Hyper-V, KVM, Sangfor) and related infrastructure components (hyperconverged infrastructure, servers, storage, networking); (iv) solid experience in IoT infrastructure, container technologies and backup and recovery systems (covering hardware, software and applications); (v) strong technical knowledge of common TCP/IP protocols (e.g. SMTP, LDAP, DNS, and DHCP) and operating systems (Linux and Windows); (vi) knowledge of information security, business continuity, and risk management; (vii) strong organizational and project management skills to handle multiple projects and meet deadlines; (viii) good customer service attitude and customer service experience; and (ix) excellent written and verbal communication skills. Candidates with less/more experience will be considered for appointment at a relevant rank. Salary and Fringe Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only . We are an equal opportunities employer . Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified . Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3027?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Philosophy",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, Department of Philosophy Hong Kong, China | req3027 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/11/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Assistant Professor Department of Philosophy (Post Ref.: 26/177) The Department of Philosophy at Lingnan University is one of the best in Asia for the study and research of analytic philosophy. More information on the research interests and publications of philosophers at Lingnan University can be found at: https://www.ln.edu.hk/philoso . General Requirements The department is interested in hiring a new Assistant Professor in ethics (broadly understood to include value theory, normative ethics, metaethics, and applied ethics) or in philosophy of AI. Candidates should have obtained, or be about to be awarded, a PhD in Philosophy, and possess a strong track record of publications in the top journals in the field. Candidates without publications will not be considered. The appointee is expected to produce internationally excellent research and obtain competitively awarded research grants. Teaching experience at the undergraduate or taught master’s level will be an advantage. The appointee is also expected to have a strong commitment to teaching excellence and to design and offer courses in their area of expertise. The teaching load will normally be four courses per year, which may be reduced under various circumstances, e.g. on receipt of external research funding or due to graduate supervision. English is the language of instruction with the possible exception of courses in Chinese philosophy. Appointment The conditions of appointment will be competitive. Commencing salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The minimum basic salary is over HKD 934,000 / USD 120,000 per year on the current salary scale. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, gratuity, and incoming passage and baggage allowance for the eligible appointee. Appointment will normally be made on an initial contract of three years, which, subject to review and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment with the possibility of consideration for substantiation (i.e., tenure). The preferred commencement date is January 2027, with a later start negotiable. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Applicants should submit the following documents: (1) a curriculum vitae; (2) a cover letter; (3) one writing sample; (4) a teaching portfolio (including syllabi of courses taught or willing to teach, and course evaluations, if any); (5) a research statement (describing past and current research, future research plans, and plans for applying for external research grants); and (6) the names and contact information of three referees (who will be contacted if the candidate is shortlisted). Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will begin on 20 July 2026 and continue until the internal selection panel has identified a list of candidates. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. For strictly clarificatory questions regarding the application procedure, candidates may contact Prof. Andrea Sauchelli (andreasauchelli@ln.edu.hk). The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/2987?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Programme Manager I, Division of Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Programme Manager I, Division of Artificial Intelligence Hong Kong, China | req2987 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/9/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Assistant Programme Manager I Division of Artificial Intelligence (Post Ref.: 26/138) Responsibilities The position is for Doctor of Artificial Intelligence Studies (DAIS) Program and the appointee is expected to: • Lead and manage overall programme administration and operations, ensuring smooth delivery of teaching and learning activities • Manage course scheduling, timetabling, and coordination of teaching activities to ensure alignment with the needs of high-profile students • Oversee end to end class and event logistics, including on-site arrangements, attendance checking, catering, and accommodation (if necessary) • Manage programme budgeting, procurement, reimbursement, and financial compliance related to programme activities • Drive programme quality assurance, including preparing programme reports and data for internal reviews and external reporting • Build and maintain strong relationships with students, faculty, and external stakeholders to support programme engagement and development • Plan and coordinate experiential learning activities to enhance students’ applied learning experience • Organize outreach and engagement events (e.g. alumni gatherings, industry talks), and external partnership activities to strengthen programme visibility and connectivity • Plan and coordinate promotional initiatives and marketing activities to support programme branding • Supervise and mentor junior administrative staff, ensuring effective teamwork and professional development • Undertake project-based and ad hoc duties as assigned by supervisors, including cross institutional collaborations Requirements • A recognized bachelor’s degree, and Master’s degree is more preferable, preferably with relevant experience in the tertiary education sector or executive education programmes • At least eight years of relevant experience with proven ability to independently manage programme or project operations • Strong programme and project management skills, with the ability to multitask, prioritize effectively, and operate under pressure in a fast‑paced environment • Self‑motivated, proactive, and able to take ownership of diverse responsibilities with a positive and professional attitude • Strong analytical and problem‑solving skills, capable of working independently and delivering high‑quality outcomes • Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua) • Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build and maintain effective relationships with diverse stakeholders Salary and Benefits The commencing salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
    "https://lingnan.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/3018?c=lingnan": {
      "title": "Assistant Administrative Officer, Dr Raymond Wong Research Centre for Arts Technology and Business",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Administrative Officer, Dr Raymond Wong Research Centre for Arts Technology and Business Hong Kong, China | req3018 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/5/2026 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Assistant Administrative Officer Dr Raymond Wong Research Centre for Arts Technology and Business (Post Ref.: 26/169 ) Responsibilities • Providing assistance in course preparation • Attendance to evening classes and/or daytime classes as assigned • Facilitating small team discussion under the supervision of the course instructors • Coordinating various student activities • Work closely with a team of teaching staff on a large-scale course, be responsible for practical and day-to-day aspects of course coordination, and support lectures on course delivery and assessment • Performing other administrative duties as assigned Requirements • A bachelor’s degree or above, preferably a Master’s degree • Good command of both English and Mandarin • Excellent interpersonal, organizational skills and communication skills with ability to work independently • Passionate in student caring are required • Proactive, willing and capable to handle projects • Having an understanding of the Taught Postgraduate Programme would be a plus • Immediate availability will be an advantage The appointee will work in the main campus and Satellite Campus Venues (Lingnan@WestKowloon), and may need to work outside normal office hours, including evenings and weekends. Salary and Benefits The commencing salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits and mandatory provident fund. Appointment will be normally made on a contract for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and the Centre’s operational need. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the posts advertised, or to fill the posts by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
