ing various full-time academic programmes including Associate Degree, Higher Diploma, Diploma, Diploma of Applied Education, Applied Learning and part-time professional continuing education programmes to meet the diverse learning needs of society. We are now inviting applications for the following subject areas of Associate Degree, Higher Diploma, Diploma programmes . 1. Accounting and Finance (Post Ref: 26/70) 2. Chinese Language and Putonghua (Post Ref: 26/71) 3. English (General English/ Academic English/ Business English/IELTS/ Language Arts and Drama) (Post Ref: 26/72) 4. General Education (Ethics/Morality/Logic) (Post Ref: 26/73) 5. Global Business (Post Ref: 26/74) 6. History (Post Ref: 26/75) 7. Literature and Romance (Post Ref: 26/76) 8. Marketing (Post Ref: 26/77) 9. Organizational Behaviour (Post Ref: 26/78) 10. Programming (Python) (Post Ref: 26/79) 11. Psychology (Post Ref: 26/80) 12. Quantitative Skills (Post Ref: 26/81) 13. Sports Coaching/Management (Post Ref: 26/82) General Requirements - A Master’s degree or above in a relevant discipline - Substantial relevant teaching experience in the tertiary education sector - May be required to teach on Saturdays For Post (2) - A native or near-native mastery of Putonghua proficiency in the respective subjects, preferably with qualification in PSC Putonghua Proficiency Test at Grade A Level 2 or above For Post (13) - Applicants should have elementary or above coaching license(s) from sports association(s) Appointment The conditions of appointment will be competitive. Remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application Procedure (online application only) Please quote the reference number of the post in the cover letter and click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application by 15 April 2026 . Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. The review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
    },
