ide a wide range of administrative support to the Division of Artificial Intelligence • Prepare reports and proposals • Provide secretarial support to various committees • Handle purchases, reimbursement, payments and other financial and budgeting matters • Liaise with internal and external parties • Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor Requirements • A recognized Bachelor’s degree with relevant experience in the tertiary education sector; For Senior Administrative Officer, the candidate should have at least four years of relevant working experience • An excellent command of written and verbal English and Chinese (including Putonghua) • High level of competence in computer literacy • Excellent analytical, organizational, interpersonal, communication and problem-solving skills • Strong sense of responsibility Salary and Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the posts advertised, or to fill the posts by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
