      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Programme Officer / Programme Officer, Division of Industrial Data Science Hong Kong, China | req2737 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/9/2025 Back to Search Lingnan University is one of the eight publicly funded institutions in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (HKSAR) and has the longest established tradition among the local institutions of higher education. It is widely recognised for providing quality education with a focus on whole-person development and conducting high-impact research for a better world. Moving forward, Lingnan University is well positioned to take lead as a comprehensive university in arts and sciences in the digital era, with impactful research and innovations. Lingnan University offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate, and research postgraduate programmes in the Faculties of Arts, Business, Social Sciences, and the Schools of Data Science, Graduate Studies and Interdisciplinary Studies. To foster interdisciplinary collaboration and scientific progress, Lingnan University established the Lingnan University Institute for Advanced Study (LUIAS), attracting distinguished scholars from around the world to collaborate with its faculty and students. With traditional strengths in arts, business, social sciences, and interdisciplinary studies, the University aims to equip students with practical knowledge and critical thinking skills to thrive in the future. Subsequent to the establishment of the School of Data Science and LUIAS, Lingnan University is transforming into a hub for global leaders to develop and promote human-centric technology and social policies. Further information about Lingnan University is available at https://www.ln.edu.hk/ . Applications are now invited for the following post: Senior Programme Officer / Programme Officer Division of Industrial Data Science (Post Ref.: 25/175) Responsibilities The appointee is expected to: • Provide administrative and promotional support for academic taught and research programs • Assist in preparing promotional materials and publications, manage and update websites and social media platforms to enhance communication and promotion • Lead content creation and dissemination, including writing articles and conducting social media campaigns to achieve high media exposure and engagement • Plan and organize related events such as seminars, conferences, exhibitions, and information days • Perform any other duties as assigned by the Person in Charge of the Division of Industrial Data Science or his/her delegates Requirements • A recognized bachelor's degree in marketing, public relations, event management, business administration or other related areas, along with relevant work experience; for the Senior Programme Officer rank, candidates should have at least four years of relevant work experience • Strong communication and interpersonal skills • Good computer literacy, including proficiency in PowerPoint, Adobe Creative Suite, and Chinese word processing • Strong problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities simultaneously • Preference will be given to those with solid knowledge of the tertiary education sector in Hong Kong and the Mainland China Salary and Benefits The rank and commencing salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, where applicable, include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, mandatory provident fund, and gratuity. Application Procedure (online application only) Please click \" Apply Now \" to submit your application. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. We are an equal opportunities employer. Review of applications will continue until the post is filled. Qualified candidates are advised to submit their applications early for consideration. The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, or to fill the post by invitation or by search. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Apply Now Share Save Job Lingnan University is an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Moreover, the anti-discrimination laws in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region (namely Sex Discrimination Ordinance, Disability Discrimination Ordinance, Family Status Discrimination Ordinance and Race Discrimination Ordinance) forbid discrimination and victimization in employment on the grounds of sex, marital status, pregnancy, disability, family status, race and the like. It is unlawful to decide against a candidate on the aforesaid grounds. Enquiries: recruit@LN.edu.hk"
